          "path": "_m/u/s/w/0/horn-ya-finnmark-wp/vard-vard-ya-finnmark-norway-m.jpg",
          "filename": "VARDØ Vardøya Finnmark NORWAY Mittet Luftfoto aerial photo 1960s Vardøhus Fortress town hall church landscape harbour fiskehjell Vestervågen Reinøya etc Nasjonalbiblioteket URN NBN no-nb digifoto 20171101 00046 NB MIT 30 013.jpg",
          "caption": "Aerial photo taken on a sunny summer day in the 1960s of the small town of Vardø in Finnmark county, Norway, located on the island of Vardøya near the Russian border. \nThe picture shows fishing boats, vessels, and quay facilities in the harbor areas of the bay, as well as houses and buildings in the town, including Vardø Church, the town hall, and the school. There are several drying racks for the production of stockfish. In the background is the island of Reinøya.\nThe port of Vardø, on the Barents Sea, remains ice-free all year round thanks to the warm North Atlantic drift. Vardø has a tundra climate, that borders on a subarctic climate.",
          "alt": "Aerial photo taken on a sunny summer day in the 1960s of the small town of Vardø in Finnmark county, Norway, located on the island of Vardøya near the Russian border. \nThe picture shows fishing boats, vessels, and quay facilities in the harbor areas of the bay, as well as houses and buildings in the town, including Vardø Church, the town hall, and the school. There are several drying racks for the production of stockfish. In the background is the island of Reinøya.\nThe port of Vardø, on the Barents Sea, remains ice-free all year round thanks to the warm North Atlantic drift. Vardø has a tundra climate, that borders on a subarctic climate.",
